# REEFER storefront — production build config.
#
# Backend: ash-ai-backend (ASH AI API), Bearer-token auth.
#
# The storefront is mounted as an isolated module at /api/storefront, with its routes in
# routes/storefront.php and its own /v1 prefix inside. Every service module in src/api/
# appends /v1/..., so this base must stop at /api/storefront:
#
#     /api/storefront/v1/products
#     /api/storefront/v1/auth/login
#
# Do NOT put /v1 on the end here — the service modules add it and it would double.
#
# The ERP's own API is /api/v2/* — a separate surface with separate accounts. Nothing in
# this app should call it.
#
# REQUIRES the storefront module to be deployed to that host. It lives on the branch
# feat/reefer-storefront; production `main` does not have it, so until that is deployed
# every call from here 404s.
#
# Vite inlines VITE_* at BUILD time, and the GitHub Actions deploy builds from this file
# — so it must stay committed, and a change needs a rebuild rather than a restart.
VITE_API_URL=https://api.sorbetesapparel.com/api/storefront
